depgraph, sets: match one atom against one package without a package set

Sub-series: E (single-atom lookups) - patch 1 of 1; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.

The resolver asks "does this one atom match this package" by building an
InternalPackageSet of one atom and calling findAtomForPackage(), and it
asks the argument, --exclude and similar sets about every package although
they hold nothing for almost every cp. _find_single_atom() answers the
first question with one match_from_list() call, with the same steps as the
set (modified USE copy, cp test). PackageSet.findAtomForPackage() and
iterAtomsForPackage() return at once when the set has no atom for the cp,
and match a lone atom once instead of twice; _iter_atoms_for_pkg() returns
an empty iterator in the same case. Two upstream commits made after
3.0.83 are included unchanged: 98f5b2293 (ExtendedAtomDict.get without
raising KeyError) and 969bcd5b7 (single match in findAtomForPackage).

On top of patches 0001-0014, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 37.6 -> 34.2, holds 19.7 -> 18.0, masks 42.0 -> 36.9,
  py313 23.1 -> 21.5, bdeps 28.3 -> 25.4, policykit 20.1 -> 18.4
  sum of six 170.8 -> 154.4 (-16.4 s, -3.7 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0015 together: 447.5 -> 154.4 s (-65 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
